LAMMPS (30 Mar 2026)
KOKKOS mode with Kokkos version 5.0.2 is enabled
  using double precision
  using view layout = legacy
  will use up to 1 GPU(s) per node
  using 1 OpenMP thread(s) per MPI task
package kokkos
package kokkos newton on neigh half
# Test 1b: single-point energy and forces of the compiled model on each frame written by model_check.py prepare.
# Run with -var frames "<i j k ...>" (the list in frames.txt). Appends "frame PE pxx pyy pzz pyz pxz pxy" (eV, bar;
# velocities are zero, so the pressure is the virial alone) to lammps_energies.txt
# and writes forces_<frame>.dump (id fx fy fz), all in the current directory, which must hold frame_<i>.data.
# Optional: -var root <project root> (default ../.., i.e. run from tests/model_check), -var model <file>.

variable        root  index ../..
variable        model index ${root}/models/run5_ep301.nequip.pt2
variable        model index ../../models/run5_ep301.nequip.pt2
variable        dt    index 0.001
variable        f     index ${frames}
variable        f     index 0 767 800 1003 1005 1131 1270 1303 1507 1508 1541 1663 2013
shell           rm -f lammps_energies.txt

label           loop
clear
  using 1 OpenMP thread(s) per MPI task
package kokkos
package kokkos newton on neigh half
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p
read_data       frame_${f}.data
read_data       frame_0.data
Reading data file ...
  triclinic box = (0 0 0) to (17.130452 14.835408 17.513606) with tilt (-8.5652261 0 0)
WARNING: Triclinic box skew is large. LAMMPS will run inefficiently. (src/domain.cpp:221)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  144 atoms
  read_data CPU = 0.031 seconds
include         ${root}/common/in.potential
include         ../../common/in.potential
# Shared potential, neighbor and group setup for every run in this project.
# Include after read_data / read_restart. Caller must define:
#   model   path to the compiled Allegro model (models/run5_ep301.nequip.pt2)
#   dt      timestep in ps (production value: common/defaults.sh; justified by tests/RESULTS.md, 1c)
# Type order is fixed by the model: 1 Ge, 2 Sb, 3 Te, 4 C (type 4 exists even when there is no C).

newton          on

pair_style      allegro
pair_coeff      * * ${model} Ge Sb Te C     # model cutoff 6.0 A
pair_coeff      * * ../../models/run5_ep301.nequip.pt2 Ge Sb Te C     

neighbor        1.0 bin
neigh_modify    delay 0 every 1 check yes
comm_modify     cutoff 7.5                  # ghost shell >= 6.0 A RDF range + 1.0 A skin

group           Ge type 1
32 atoms in group Ge
group           Sb type 2
32 atoms in group Sb
group           Te type 3
80 atoms in group Te
group           C  type 4
0 atoms in group C
variable        nC equal count(C)

timestep        ${dt}
timestep        0.001
thermo_style    custom step pe pxx pyy pzz pyz pxz pxy
dump            fr all custom 1 forces_${f}.dump id fx fy fz
dump            fr all custom 1 forces_0.dump id fx fy fz
dump_modify     fr sort id format float %20.12g
run             0

